<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Guelph Trees &mdash; OSM Coverage Gaps</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../index.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="gaps.css">
<link rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css"
      integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY="
      crossorigin="">
<script defer src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js"
        integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo="
        crossorigin=""></script>
<script defer src="gaps.js"></script>
</head>
<body class="app">

<header class="bar">
  <div class="bar-head">
    <h1>Guelph Trees &mdash; OSM coverage gaps</h1>
    <a class="back" href="../">&larr; reference layer</a>
    <a class="back" href="history.html">gaps over time &rarr;</a>
  </div>
  <div class="counts">
    <div class="count empty_cell"><strong>{{EMPTY_CELL_COUNT}}</strong><span>{{CELL_M}}&nbsp;m cells with no OSM tree</span></div>
    <div class="count thin_cell"><strong>{{THIN_CELL_COUNT}}</strong><span>thin cells (under {{THIN_PCT}}% matched)</span></div>
    <div class="count missing"><strong>{{MISSING_COUNT}}</strong><span>City trees with no OSM tree within {{MATCH_M}}&nbsp;m</span></div>
    <div class="count nospecies"><strong>{{NOSPECIES_COUNT}}</strong><span>matched OSM trees without species</span></div>
    <div class="count nogirth"><strong>{{NOGIRTH_COUNT}}</strong><span>without girth</span></div>
    <div class="count"><strong>{{CITY_COUNT}}</strong><span>City trees</span></div>
    <div class="count"><strong>{{OSM_COUNT}}</strong><span>OSM trees</span></div>
    <div class="count matched"><strong>{{MATCHED_COUNT}}</strong><span>matched ({{MATCHED_PCT}}%)</span></div>
    <div class="count meta-count">City data {{DATA_DATE}} &middot; OSM data {{OSM_DATE}} &middot; compared {{BUILD_DATE}}</div>
  </div>
  {{OSM_NOTE}}
  <p class="caution">
    <strong>Add what you verify.</strong> Copying species or girth from this
    overlay into OSM is in effect an attribute import, and importing individual
    trees is contested in OSM &mdash; add what you can check yourself (a crown
    on imagery, a species on the ground); nothing here is meant to be
    bulk-copied. OSM <code>circumference</code> is in metres (DBH &times;
    &pi;&nbsp;/&nbsp;100; the City's DBH is in cm). OSM trees with no City tree
    are not listed: woodlots, back yards and campus trees the City does not
    inventory.
  </p>
  <p class="licence">
    <a href="{{LICENSE_URL}}">{{LICENSE_NOTICE}}</a>
    Source: <a href="{{DATASET_PAGE}}">Trees</a>.
  </p>
</header>

<div class="layout">
  <div id="gap-map"
       data-cells="cells.geojson"
       data-trees="trees.json"
       data-match-m="{{MATCH_M}}"
       data-raster="../tiles/raster/{z}/{x}/{y}.png"></div>

  <aside class="panel">
    <!-- Mode 1: every cell holding a City tree, most missing trees first. -->
    <div class="mode" id="cells-mode">
      <div class="panel-head">
        <div class="controls">
          <label><span class="swatch empty_cell"></span>
            <input type="checkbox" data-status="empty_cell" checked> Empty</label>
          <label><span class="swatch thin_cell"></span>
            <input type="checkbox" data-status="thin_cell" checked> Thin</label>
          <label><span class="swatch covered"></span>
            <input type="checkbox" data-status="covered" checked> Covered</label>
          <label><span class="swatch sparse"></span>
            <input type="checkbox" data-status="sparse"> Sparse</label>
          <input type="search" id="filter" placeholder="Filter by street or cell...">
        </div>
        <p class="hint">
          The City's street and park trees (raster layer), counted in
          {{CELL_M}}&nbsp;m squares. <strong>Empty</strong>: at least
          {{CELL_MIN_CITY}} City trees and no OSM tree at all.
          <strong>Thin</strong>: some OSM trees, but under {{THIN_PCT}}% of the
          City trees have one within {{MATCH_M}}&nbsp;m. <strong>Covered</strong>:
          the rest &mdash; there may still be species or girth to add.
          <strong>Sparse</strong>: fewer than {{CELL_MIN_CITY}} City trees. Click
          a cell or a row to list its trees.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table class="gap-table" id="cell-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Cell</th><th class="num">City</th><th class="num">OSM</th>
                <th class="num">Missing</th><th class="num">No species</th>
                <th>Status</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Mode 2: one cell's trees that need something. -->
    <div class="mode" id="cell-mode" hidden>
      <div class="panel-head">
        <a class="back-cells" href="#" id="back-cells">&larr; all cells</a>
        <h2 id="cell-title"></h2>
        <p class="cell-counts" id="cell-counts"></p>
        <div class="controls key">
          <span><span class="swatch t-missing"></span> no OSM tree within {{MATCH_M}}&nbsp;m</span>
          <span><span class="swatch t-species"></span> OSM tree lacks species</span>
          <span><span class="swatch t-girth"></span> lacks girth only</span>
        </div>
        <p class="hint">
          Click a row to zoom to the tree, then press <kbd>O</kbd> to open it on
          openstreetmap.org or <kbd>I</kbd> in the iD editor (each row has the
          same <strong>OSM&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;iD</strong> link pair; with no
          tree picked the keys open the cell). A matched tree links to its OSM
          node, a missing one to the City's position. Matched trees that already
          carry species and girth are not listed.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <p class="table-note" id="tree-note" hidden></p>
        <table class="gap-table" id="tree-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Tree</th><th class="num">DBH</th>
                <th>Status</th><th>OSM &middot; iD</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </aside>
</div>

</body>
</html>
